  "family": "Painterly",
  "description": "A sheet of cold-press paper painted wet-in-wet: every object starts as an off-register pencil underdrawing, then layered washes bloom past the lines, a second colour runs through them, pigment pools dark at their edges and granulates, and white paper is kept for highlights. Labels are hand-lettered in bleeding ink. A clear-water glaze sweeps across between scenes and its drying front wipes in the next painting, while drops keep landing and blooming, rinse jars stir, a brush works the palette, a paper boat sails and painted folk talk and gesture.",
